    "summary": "Iskandar (Alexander the Great) hunting with companions. Detached folio from an illustrated manuscript of the Iskandarnama (Book of Alexander), in the Khamsa (Quintet) of Nizami, later mounted onto a detached album folio. Painting depicts depicts Alexander the Great, known as Iskandar in Persian, and his companions hunting wild fowl from boats. While Iskandar shoots from a throne on his boat, his courtiers serenade him with harp and tambourine.The illustration is surrounded by an ornate floral border and four isolated titles. Eight single-lined columns of text appear at the top and bottom of illustration.\r\n\r\nInk, opaque watercolour and gold on paper.",
